<title>ITALY: Italy's Bologna sees Jan CPI at 0.3 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Bologna sees Jan CPI at 0.3 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>BOLOGNA, Italy 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Bologna said its January consumer price index stood at 0.3 percent month-on-month and 2.9 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In December, Bologna's inflation rate was -0.3 and 3.0 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Bologna is one of 11 Italian cities which published inflation data Monday and Tuesday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 7.62 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to December 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.3  (-0.3)     2.9  (3.0)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.3  (-0.3)     0.8  (1.5)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.0   (0.0)     2.5  (2.4)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.6   (0.1)     6.7  (6.6)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.0   (0.0)     1.7  (1.5)</p>
<p>    Health services		   2.6   (0.0)     4.5  (5.0)</p>
<p>    Transportation		   -0.8   (0.2)     2.9  (2.8)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.7  (-2.1)     7.3  (7.7)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0   (0.0)     2.3  (2.6)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.6   (0.0)     2.0  (2.6)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.8   (0.1)     1.1  (0.8)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
